          "body": "`open_links` contains every linked contact from the nightly table, and this union happens before applying the contact arm's date, channel, category, type, episode, or persona-view filters. A linked old contact can therefore suppress its candidate row even when that contact does not render. For example, a contact from 40 days ago linked to a lead from 10 days ago makes a custom 14-day query return neither row: the contact fails `date_from`, while its unfiltered link removes the in-range lead.",
